  "details": "When using scaling animations with physbones, when IsAnimated is enabled, the physics seems to have issues calculating correctly and may get stuck at the max angle they are allowed to. \n\nShown avatar does have on the root transform a 1:1:1 scale and scales the first two childbones to 0.85:0.7:8.5 . When IsAnimated is disabled, it works as intended, but ingame the length of the physics is not updated, so it calculates collisions with its \"normal length\" of the bones being 1:1:1, despite the hair being short. (In debug view the bone length does not change, despite the hair getting shorter)\n\nWhen IsAnimated is enabled, the scale is updated correctly, but the physics calculation itself seems to break. This behavior is already visible in unity, so I made a video showcasing it: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0Tipdbyiqhg\nAlso, as we noticed during testing, when IsAnimated is turned on, calculations seem to allow the scale to be ignored to a certain extend, meaning the scaled bones can stretch themselves up to the original length.\n\nThis leaves one currently with two options: Either with \"IsAnimated\" on, knowing that the calculations seem to have issues or to stick with \"IsAnimated\" off, which does not update the length of the physbone ingame, leading to collisions that do not make a lot of sense happening. (For example having hair all the way to the knees will still collide with legs/hips etc, despite being shrunk all the way up the the shoulders)\n\nEdit: uploaded four screens showing that unity preview behavior is different to ingame behavior when isanimated is off, first two screens are scaled, the last two are not scaled.",
